internlm3_8b_instruct__gsm8k_train_00067_7ae2a064__temp0.10__seed7,internlm3_8b_instruct,internlm/InternLM3-8B-Instruct,gsm8k_train_00067_7ae2a064,gsm8k,grade_school_math,gsm8k,67,16,2,"Now that I have the two equations, P + C = 108 and C = 5P + 12, I can substitute the second equation into the first to solve for P. This will help me find the number of pens Issac bought.","Let's substitute C from the second equation into the first: P + (5P + 12) = 108. Simplifying this gives 6P + 12 = 108. Subtracting 12 from both sides results in 6P = 96. Dividing both sides by 6 gives P = 16. So, Issac bought 16 pens.",16,1,90,1,1,38,256,-0.10380744934082031,0.3502301573753357,1.019619107246399,16.234355926513672,5.410213470458984,0.05336141586303711,0.31746031746031744,3.46,0.95,17.5824101800099,14.560006129936381,16.430450916290283,7,0.1,cuda,minimal_json,default,0,1,json_exact,json_field,json_field,json_field,1,0,504,256,"```json
{
