internlm3_8b_instruct__gsm8k_train_00165_3ec73ad9__temp0.10__seed7,internlm3_8b_instruct,internlm/InternLM3-8B-Instruct,gsm8k_train_00165_3ec73ad9,gsm8k,grade_school_math,gsm8k,165,113,3,"Next, I'll calculate the total number of nails for the parrots, remembering that one parrot has an extra toe. Each parrot typically has three claws on each leg, and since parrots have two legs, this would be 3 claws per leg * 2 legs = 6 claws per parrot. However, one parrot has an extra toe, adding one more claw. Therefore, this parrot has 6 + 1 = 7 claws. With eight parrots, the total number of claws for the parrots is 7 claws for the special parrot plus 6 claws for each of the other seven parrots, which is 7 * 6 = 42 claws. Adding the special parrot's extra claw, the total for the parrots is 42 + 7 = 49 claws.",64 nails for the dogs and 49 claws for the parrots,49,0,70,0,1,118,256,-0.16647523641586304,0.44966989755630493,0.9673082232475281,15.882292747497559,14.075056076049805,0.3439416289329529,0.27380952380952384,3.26,-0.1,20.755102046066895,12.334316614382157,16.430450916290283,7,0.1,cuda,minimal_json,default,0,1,json_exact,json_field,json_field,json_field,1,0,753,256,"```json
{
