  ""answer"": ""To find the number of men, I will first calculate the total number of students by adding the number of women (180) to the number of men, which is 70% of the total. Let's denote the total number of students as \( T \). The equation is \( 0.70T = \text{number of men} \) and \( T - 0.70T = 180 \). Solving for \( T \) gives \( 0.30T = 180 \), so \( T = \frac{180}{0.30} = 600 \). Therefore, the number of men is \( 0.70 \times 600 = 420 \)."",
