internlm3_8b_instruct__gsm8k_train_00275_bf17b203__temp0.10__seed7,internlm3_8b_instruct,internlm/InternLM3-8B-Instruct,gsm8k_train_00275_bf17b203,gsm8k,grade_school_math,gsm8k,275,480,1,"To solve this problem, I need to determine the individual prices of shoes and jerseys. Given that jerseys cost 1/4 the price of one pair of shoes, I can set up an equation to represent the total cost. Let's denote the price of one pair of shoes as S and the price of one jersey as J. The relationship given is J = S/4. The total cost for 6 pairs of shoes and 4 jerseys is $560. So, the equation becomes 6S + 4J = 560. Substituting J with S/4 gives 6S + 4(S/4) = 560. Simplifying this equation will help me find the value of S.",The total price of the shoes is $400.,400,0,90,0,0,108,256,-0.185431569814682,0.48569411039352417,1.0545017719268799,15.549750328063965,0.0,0.0,0.0,3.46,0.0,15.736862739082426,16.267537198772484,16.430450916290283,7,0.1,cuda,minimal_json,default,0,1,json_exact,json_field,json_field,json_field,1,0,647,256,"```json
