  ""thought"": ""To solve this problem, I need to determine the individual prices of shoes and jerseys. Given that jerseys cost 1/4 the price of one pair of shoes, I can set up an equation to represent the total cost. Let's denote the price of one pair of shoes as S and the price of one jersey as J. The relationship given is J = S/4. The total cost for 6 pairs of shoes and 4 jerseys is $560. So, the equation becomes 6S + 4J = 560. Substituting J with S/4 gives 6S + 4(S/4) = 560. Simplifying this equation will help me find the value of S."",
